              "ImageDescription": {
                "source": "commons-desc-page",
                "value": "This is a 1969 environmental poster from the US federal government about controlling air pollution. The Statue of Liberty is wearing a gas mask in this poster and the poster is in a countercultural style found in the era. Exact person to designed the poster is unknown. According to the poster it was made by the US Department of Health, Education and Welfare's Public Health Service. More specifically, the National Air Pollution Control Administration under the Consumer Protection and Environmental Health Service which appears to be under the Public Health Service. Published in 1969 by the US Government Printing Office."
              },
